hi I'm Talulah Riley and I'm really  excited to be releasing my debut novel  acts of love and these are my top 5 tips  for writing something really important  is to protect your writing time fiercely  and make sure that you carve out chunks  of time where you can sit and think and  more things over and do the actual  writing and really make sure that's as  important to you as any anything else in  your diary it's really nice to have some  sort of creative inspiration for  whatever you're doing so whether that's  a particular song you listen to that you  associate with what you're writing or  the mood board or just some other  creative outlet that that mirrors the  process you're going through with your  writing and that inspires you that isn't  actually you know you always that with  your fingers on the keys I would suggest  that you not be afraid of writing and  just try and put fair in a box and  tighten up with a bone throw it away  because obviously it's a really scary  thing to do the way any creative thing  is scary but try and harness that and  use that energy as opposed to let fear  overtake you and crap lead it's really  nice to have someone that you trust a  bounce ideas off and to be your first  reader so my best friend from school  read acts of love first and was really  great about giving me constructive  criticism and you want someone that you  know will be totally honest with you but  not brutally honest so someone who will  respect the fact that what you've just  done is difficult and scary but will  give you valuable feedback  so another really important thing is to  just finish whatever you're doing I left  acts of love in a metaphorical drawer  for a year I'd written the first eight  chapters and then just didn't write the  last chapter for a year and this sort of  bothered me the whole of that year and  then when I finally took it out and  finished it there was a real sense of  achievement just in the fact that it  existed as a completed thing so even if  it doesn't feel like it's going very  well just keep going all the way through  you
 

